{
  "duration": 76.159,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.119,
      "end": 0.28,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.719,
      "end": 1.519,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.18,
      "end": 3.639,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.099,
      "end": 7.319,
      "text": "Now in this problem, we are given that two trains have the same speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.819,
      "end": 9.859,
      "text": "Train one crosses a pole in 12 seconds,"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.319,
      "end": 12.619,
      "text": "and train two crosses a pole in 18 seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.979,
      "end": 15.639,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find the ratio of their lengths."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.1,
      "end": 18.779,
      "text": "Let the speed of each train be V meter per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.219,
      "end": 21.739,
      "text": "Let the lengths of the two trains be L1 and L2."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.159,
      "end": 23.739,
      "text": "Now, the important concept here is"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.119,
      "end": 26.939,
      "text": "when a train crosses a pole, it covers only its own length."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.42,
      "end": 29.439,
      "text": "There is no platform or another train involved,"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.76,
      "end": 37.139,
      "text": "so the distance covered is simply the length of the train. Hence, we use the formula time equals length of train divided by speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.799,
      "end": 41.899,
      "text": "Since both trains have the same speed, this speed will be equal for both."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.419,
      "end": 44.279,
      "text": "So we can say L1 by"
    },
    {
      "start": 44.659,
      "end": 46.899,
      "text": "L2 equals T1 by T2."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.34,
      "end": 47.619,
      "text": "Why?"
    },
    {
      "start": 48.099,
      "end": 52.199,
      "text": "Because length is directly proportional to time when the speed remains the same."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.619,
      "end": 54.259,
      "text": "This is the main idea of the question."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.699,
      "end": 56.299,
      "text": "Now, let us put the given values,"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.979,
      "end": 57.419,
      "text": "L1 by"
    },
    {
      "start": 57.899,
      "end": 65.339,
      "text": "L2 equals 12 by 18. After simplifying this by dividing both numbers by six, we get L1 by"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.959,
      "end": 66.039,
      "text": "L2"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.54,
      "end": 68.139,
      "text": "equals two by three."
    },
    {
      "start": 68.919,
      "end": 76.159,
      "text": "So the required ratio of the lengths of the two trains is two is to three. Hence, the correct option is option B."
    }
  ],
